      "description": "Watch Barnsley vs Crewe highlights and goals from Carabao on ReFooty: Football Highlights Hub. Match played on August 25, 2026. On August 25, 2026 , the stadium crackled with anticipation for this high-stakes Carabao Cup clash. Both teams took to the pitch with clear attacking intent, setting the stage for a match defined by shifts in momentum and clinical finishing. A Rapid First-Half Turnaround The contest ignited in the 21st minute when Crewe Alexandra struck first against the run of play. A swift counter-attack saw Charlie McNeill find Adrien Thibaut , who unleashed a precise shot into the top right corner. However, the lead served only to wake the hosts. Barnsley responded with a devastating nine-minute spell that completely flipped the narrative. Reyes Cleary found the equalizer in the 29th minute, and just two minutes later, Tyrese Noslin kept his cool in the center of the box to put the home side ahead. The pressure from the Tykes didn't subside, and they extended their advantage before the break. In the 38th minute, Corey O'Keeffe picked up the ball on the left side of the area and curled a right-footed effort into the top corner. At 3-1, Barnsley looked to be in total control as the teams headed into the interval following a dominant displays of clinical attacking football. Late Drama and Heroic Saves The second half saw Barnsley push for a fourth, with Luke Alker and Patrick Kelly both denied by the impressive Tom Booth in the Crewe goal. As the clock ticked down, the visitors began to find their second wind. Charlie McNeill was denied by the woodwork in the 83rd minute, a moment that signaled a frantic finish. In the 89th minute, substitute Joel Ewusi rose highest to head home a Lewis Billington cross, reducing the deficit to a single goal and setting up a grandstand finish. Stoppage time was a test of nerves for the home supporters. Crewe Alexandra threw everything forward, forcing Rogan Ravenhill into two sensational saves to deny Adrien Thibaut and Mickey Demetriou . In the final seconds, Kyle Ure had a chance to force a shootout with a direct free kick, but his effort sailed narrowly over the bar. Barnsley held firm to secure their 3-2 victory and advance to the next round."
